.Dd August 18, 2026
.Dt LOCALE.GEN 5
.Os Sowa
.Sh NAME
.Nm locale.gen
.Nd which locales this machine compiles, and the catalogue of every one it could
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /etc/locale.gen
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa /etc/locale.gen
is read by
.Xr locale-gen 8 ,
which compiles each locale the file enables into
.Pa /usr/lib/locale/locale-archive .
Each line is
.Pp
.Dl locale charset
.Pp
where
.Ar locale
is a name such as
.Ql de_DE.UTF-8
and
.Ar charset
is the character map to compile it against, such as
.Ql UTF-8 .
Blank lines and lines beginning with
.Ql #
are ignored.
.Pp
The file ships holding every locale the C library it was built against
supports - a little over five hundred of them, generated from glibc's own
.Pa localedata/SUPPORTED -
with all but the image's own set commented out.
So it is a catalogue as much as a configuration: the way to find a name is to
search this file.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
grep -i portuguese /etc/locale.gen
grep '^#pt_' /etc/locale.gen
.Ed
.Pp
A locale is enabled by uncommenting its line, or by naming it to
.Xr locale-gen 8 ,
which uncomments it and then compiles.
Neither the file nor the archive is consulted by any program at run time except
.Xr locale-gen 8 :
what a program sees is the compiled archive, so an edit here does nothing until
.Xr locale-gen 8
has run.
.Pp
The image is built with the set in
.Pa config/locales.conf
in the Sowa source tree, which is the same two lines this file arrives with
uncommented.
.Sh THE COST OF A LOCALE
Compiled locales share their character tables and pay separately for collation
and formats, so the first one is expensive and the rest are not.
.Ql C.UTF-8
alone is 392 KB;
with
.Ql en_US.UTF-8
beside it, 2.9 MB;
sixteen locales covering most of the world's speakers, 17 MB;
all 328 UTF-8 locales, about 200 MB.
An installed system that wants them all can have them:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sed -i 's/^#\e([a-z].*UTF-8\e)$/\e1/' /etc/locale.gen
locale-gen
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/lib/locale/locale-archive"
.It Pa /etc/locale.gen
This file.
.It Pa /usr/lib/locale/locale-archive
What
.Xr locale-gen 8
writes from it.
.It Pa /usr/share/i18n/locales
The locale definitions, one file per locale, in the source form
.Xr localedef 1
reads.
.It Pa /usr/share/i18n/charmaps
The character maps.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr locale 1 ,
.Xr localedef 1 ,
.Xr locale.conf 5 ,
.Xr locale-gen 8
.Pp
.Pa /root/sowa-howto/locale.txt
